<title>USA: Fed buys coupons from 8/31/98 to 2/15/00.</title>
<headline>Fed buys coupons from 8/31/98 to 2/15/00.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added permanent reserves to the U.S. banking system on Wednesday via a coupon pass, a Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>The Fed bought coupons from August 31, 1998 to February 15, 2000 for delivery on Thursday, the Fed said.</p>
<p>U.S. money market analysts had said the Fed might add permanent reserves to the banking system at any time.</p>
<p>(( -- John Hughes, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1663 ))</p>
